# kk: Disable KK_WORKAROUND_10 on M3+
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45951 state=merged
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

In bcsel, the extra true is no longer needed to avoid the compiler error. The error happened on M1 and M2. On M3+ it no longer happens.

Changed one line in kk_physical_device.c, inside the M3+ workarounds block. Added new condition for M3+ (`gpu_apple_family >= 9`). Added a new line in the Log section of the KK_WORKAROUND_10 entry in workarounds.rst.

* CTS: 56,319 subgroups, glsl, spirv and draw tests. Results were exactly the same with the workaround enabled and disabled: 9,402 Pass, 6 Fail and 6 DeviceLost that already existed before, and the rest NotSupported. This includes the subgroupinclusive\*\_vec4 tests, which were the ones originally failing, and they pass.
* Hardware: M5 Pro, macOS 27.2.
* Improvement: in a heavy game in a PS5 emulator, with the workaround, compiling large compute shaders took about 3 times longer, and the game froze while compiling.

Assisted-by: LLM 

Original Language: ESP
